# Fraktal/AB host adapter arguments: one option or value per line.
#
# Optional, one per instance. Put a host_adapter.args beside an instance's
# gateway.args to run the host adapter for the same PLC:
#   %LOCALAPPDATA%\Fraktal\Gateway\instances\<name>\host_adapter.args
# The tray starts it with the gateway, restarts it on its own backoff and
# logs it to logs\<name>\host_adapter.log. No file means no adapter: a
# PLC-memory-only station runs none.
#
# The adapter answers the jobs a V6.11 controller opens for its configuration
# sets and live documents. It keeps the four named sets in
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\Fraktal\ConfigSets\<serial>-<root> (override with
# FRAKTAL_AB_CONFIG_SET_DIR), live documents in its live\ folder, and host
# events in events\host_events.jsonl with their cursor in events\cursor.json.
# A restore runs under the logged-in operator's authority: it gains no login
# and no write path that operator does not have.
--host
192.168.1.10
--slot
0
# The controller's exact eight-hex serial: the adapter refuses any other.
--expect-serial
00000000
